WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.733
A vector records a directed change, not merely the location of its drawn tip

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:09.162
One, two means one unit right and two up

00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:16.400
Two, negative one means two right and one down; moving an arrow without changing its displacement preserves the vector.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.237
Add vectors component by component because horizontal and vertical changes combine independently

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:29.235
The total horizontal change is three and the total vertical change is one

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:35.233
Placing the second movement after the first would reach the same resulting displacement.

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.441
Scalar multiplication changes every component by the same factor

00:00:40.441 --> 00:00:44.783
Doubling this vector doubles its length while keeping its direction

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:53.033
A negative multiplier reverses direction as well; in general the new length uses the absolute value of the scalar.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:59.476
The dot product measures alignment by adding products of matching components

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:02.282
These two contributions cancel to zero

00:01:02.282 --> 00:01:12.100
Since both vectors are nonzero, zero dot product means the vectors are perpendicular, connecting coordinate arithmetic with a geometric right angle.
